<h1>💍 Marriage Lesson 7: Financial Stewardship in Marriage</h1>

<h2>Key Text</h2>

<p>
"Moreover it is required in stewards, that a man be found faithful."
<br><br>
<strong>1 Corinthians 4:2</strong>
</p>

<h2>Introduction</h2>

<p>
Money is one of the areas that can either strengthen or weaken a marriage. Many family conflicts arise from poor financial management, lack of planning, or disagreements about spending.
</p>

<p>
God calls married couples to be faithful stewards of the resources He provides.
</p>

<h2>God Owns Everything</h2>

<p>
The Bible teaches that everything belongs to God. Our money, possessions, talents, and opportunities are gifts entrusted to us by Him.
</p>

<p>
As stewards, husbands and wives should manage finances wisely and responsibly.
</p>

<h2>Financial Unity</h2>

<p>
Marriage is a partnership. Couples should work together when making financial decisions rather than acting independently.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Discuss financial goals together.</li>
<li>Create a family budget.</li>
<li>Be transparent about spending.</li>
<li>Avoid financial secrets.</li>
<li>Pray together about major decisions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The Importance of Budgeting</h2>

<p>
A budget helps families use resources wisely and avoid unnecessary debt.
</p>

<p>
Good budgeting allows couples to meet needs, save for the future, support God's work, and prepare for emergencies.
</p>

<h2>Avoiding Debt</h2>

<p>
While some financial obligations may be unavoidable, unnecessary debt can place stress on a marriage.
</p>

<p>
Wise couples live within their means and avoid spending beyond what they can afford.
</p>

<h2>Giving and Generosity</h2>

<p>
Christian families should honor God through faithful giving. Returning tithes and offerings is an act of worship and gratitude.
</p>

<p>
Generosity also reflects God's character and blesses others.
</p>

<h2>Contentment and Gratitude</h2>

<p>
Many financial problems come from comparing ourselves with others. God's Word teaches contentment and gratitude for His blessings.
</p>

<p>
A content family experiences greater peace and joy than one constantly chasing material possessions.
</p>

<h2>Working Together Toward Goals</h2>

<p>
Successful couples establish common financial goals such as:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Saving for future needs.</li>
<li>Supporting children's education.</li>
<li>Reducing debt.</li>
<li>Helping others.</li>
<li>Advancing God's mission.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Memory Verse</h2>

<p>
